<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · infrastructure</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nelson's Dockyard</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">18th century</span> · Also known as English Harbour Dockyard</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nelson's Dockyard is the Georgian naval dockyard at English Harbour in Antigua, built in the 18th century as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-navy">Royal Navy</a>'s chief base in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leeward-islands">Leeward Islands</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/horatio-nelson">Horatio Nelson</a> served there in the 1780s. Closed in 1889, it was restored in the 20th century and is now a heritage site and marina, inscribed on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco">UNESCO</a> World Heritage List in 2016.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nelsons-dockyard.jpg" alt="Nelson's Dockyard" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: David Stanley · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nelson%27s_Dockyard.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
